  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (cut from upstream/main 37482923).\n\nAdds `site/content/guide/migrating.md` (\"Coming from another CAM system\", weight 7, after Refusals). No other CAM product is named and the page states CamCraft reads no other system's tool, project or post files (#300).\n\nSections: Tools (library file and fields, worked CSV -> camcraft-tools example with a Python script, import modes Add/Update/Replace and the report, holders, check before cutting); Models (STEP/STL/OBJ, 25.4x unit check, STEP facet budget); Machines and posts; Concepts; What does not migrate; First-job checklist.\n\nSources checked: crates/app/src/tool_library.rs (envelope, refusals), project/file.rs ToolDto/ToolKindDto (field names), tools.rs is_sane (diameter and corner_r limits), docs/decisions/899-tool-import-modes.md and ui pages.rs (mode labels), assets/scripts/cam.d.ts (importTools/exportTools/import), geometry/import (MAX_FACETS 30M, step_budget MIN/CEILING), docs/user-guide/vendor-fixtures.md, docs/MACHINE-ONBOARDING.md, existing guide pages.\n\nNot on main / not covered: no import of other systems' formats (by decision); the CLI examples section of the issue is not in this PR (follow-up); the facet budget has no GUI control documented, only the script/MCP argument.\n\nNot exercised: no zola in this environment, so `zola check` was not run; the worked JSON was checked as valid JSON with matching field names but not fed through the app's importer; links use the `@/guide/` internal form of sibling pages.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1240\n",
